0226: warm starts from the shader cache (issue #6: "Preparing shaders" on every start)

- Statistics for the startup hold (aurora_pipeline_cache_get_stats): Dawn blob cache hits, misses,
  stores, time in lookups/stores, entries at open, session count, whether the file is unusable;
  GX pipeline creation time by stage (WGSL generation, shader module, render pipeline); the
  rebuild count and whether the enhanced-lighting prewarm still runs. The application uses them
  to start the game once a sample of the startup batch loaded without a single compile, and to
  say whether shaders are loaded or compiled.
- Age-based prune of dawn_cache.db: entries are dropped after 5 launches unused (session counter
  table aurora_session, column last_used added to existing caches), not at the first launch that
  did not need them. Switching graphics settings deleted every blob of the other settings, and
  blobs first read after the prune (late pipelines) were deleted at every launch.
- PRAGMA quick_check on dawn_cache.db / pipeline_cache.db only after an unclean exit (crash
  journal): it read the whole 60-250 MB file before the first pipeline, 2.2 s for 244 MB from an
  NVMe SSD after a reboot. Instead the file is read sequentially on a background thread into the
  OS file cache (237 ms), so the random blob lookups do not each wait for the disk.

